1
00:00:02,293 --> 00:00:03,461
<i>Something to cool your head.</i>

2
00:00:04,546 --> 00:00:05,714
[JORDAN] <i>I'm sorry, dude.</i>

3
00:00:07,048 --> 00:00:09,467
<i>I just don't want you to experience</i>
<i>what happened with my mom.</i>

4
00:00:10,343 --> 00:00:11,386
<i>They still haven't caught</i>

5
00:00:11,469 --> 00:00:12,971
<i>the hit-and-run driver who hit her.</i>

6
00:00:13,054 --> 00:00:14,931
<i>That's why I want Caloy to be caught.</i>

7
00:00:15,557 --> 00:00:17,392
<i>And for Bea to be held accountable.</i>

8
00:00:17,475 --> 00:00:19,269
<i>They have to pay for what they did.</i>

9
00:00:25,150 --> 00:00:26,276
[ROBBIE] <i>Boss.</i>

10
00:00:26,359 --> 00:00:27,610
<i>I think you've had too much to drink.</i>

11
00:00:28,611 --> 00:00:29,696
<i>You know,</i>

12
00:00:30,405 --> 00:00:31,614
<i>I was young</i>

13
00:00:31,698 --> 00:00:33,074
<i>when I lost my mom.</i>

14
00:00:36,995 --> 00:00:38,204
<i>And Grandpa…</i>

15
00:00:39,539 --> 00:00:42,000
<i>With his condition,</i>
<i>I feel like I'm losing him too.</i>

16
00:00:44,586 --> 00:00:45,712
<i>And now Billy.</i>

17
00:00:49,132 --> 00:00:50,300
<i>I nearly lost her.</i>

18
00:00:51,676 --> 00:00:53,386
<i>But she's safe, isn't she?</i>

19
00:00:55,764 --> 00:00:57,098
<i>I just realized</i>

20
00:00:58,141 --> 00:01:00,018
<i>how important she is to me.</i>

21
00:01:02,687 --> 00:01:03,980
<i>I knew it.</i>

22
00:01:04,564 --> 00:01:06,107
<i>She's like my family.</i>

23
00:01:07,150 --> 00:01:09,652
<i>Her, Oliver, and Auntie Pres.</i>

24
00:01:11,821 --> 00:01:13,865
<i>Ever since we were in high school,</i>

25
00:01:13,948 --> 00:01:15,533
<i>whenever Grandpa had a gig,</i>

26
00:01:16,367 --> 00:01:19,204
<i>he'd leave me at Billy's house.</i>

27
00:01:21,122 --> 00:01:24,375
<i>Dude, you're eating three pieces?!</i>
<i>Save some for the rest of us!</i>

28
00:01:24,459 --> 00:01:26,127
<i>This came from my grandpa, right?</i>

29
00:01:26,211 --> 00:01:28,004
<i>Fine. Have as much as you want.</i>

30
00:01:28,087 --> 00:01:29,088
<i>Oh, I'm sorry.</i>

31
00:01:31,007 --> 00:01:33,384
<i>- I don't like that.</i>
<i>- Oh yeah!</i>

32
00:01:33,468 --> 00:01:35,553
<i>You like the drumsticks.</i>

33
00:01:37,555 --> 00:01:38,473
<i>Peace.</i>

34
00:01:39,891 --> 00:01:41,851
<i>Fine. We're good now.</i>

35
00:01:42,435 --> 00:01:45,897
<i>Didn't I tell you yesterday</i>
<i>that I wasn't available?</i>

36
00:01:45,980 --> 00:01:48,149
<i>You know, you just wasted my time.</i>

37
00:01:48,233 --> 00:01:49,651
<i>That's not true!</i>

38
00:01:49,734 --> 00:01:51,111
<i>If it's not true, let's go.</i>

39
00:01:51,194 --> 00:01:53,947
<i>- Come with me. Let's go.</i>
<i>- Brandon, that hurts!</i>

40
00:01:54,030 --> 00:01:54,864
<i>Bro.</i>

41
00:01:54,948 --> 00:01:57,325
<i>Don't force her to come</i>
<i>if she doesn't want to.</i>

42
00:01:58,201 --> 00:01:59,536
<i>You should go.</i>

43
00:01:59,619 --> 00:02:01,621
<i>I'll call security if you don't.</i>

44
00:02:04,749 --> 00:02:06,417
[BEA]<i> I also have a background</i>
<i>in marketing,</i>

45
00:02:06,501 --> 00:02:08,169
<i>sales, and computer programming.</i>

46
00:02:08,253 --> 00:02:12,006
<i>I am certain, ma'am, that I am qualified</i>
<i>for the executive assistant position.</i>

47
00:02:13,466 --> 00:02:14,968
[HR OFFICER]
<i>Hmm… Okay.</i>

48
00:02:15,051 --> 00:02:18,429
<i>We'll consider your application</i>
<i>and call you.</i>

49
00:02:22,142 --> 00:02:23,309
[CALOY] <i>Hey!</i>

50
00:02:25,061 --> 00:02:26,271
<i>Caloy?!</i>

51
00:02:28,857 --> 00:02:29,858
[BEA] You…

52
00:02:30,358 --> 00:02:32,193
Why did you come here?

53
00:02:32,777 --> 00:02:34,487
Someone might recognize you.

54
00:02:34,571 --> 00:02:36,114
You know it's dangerous.

55
00:02:36,197 --> 00:02:39,117
[CHUCKLES] Even you didn't recognize me.

56
00:02:39,993 --> 00:02:41,452
Right?

57
00:02:41,536 --> 00:02:42,662
I'm pretty good, aren't I?

58
00:02:42,745 --> 00:02:44,664
[CALOY CHUCKLES] I'm really good.

59
00:02:45,790 --> 00:02:46,708
You--

60
00:02:47,333 --> 00:02:48,918
You don't have to worry.

61
00:02:49,002 --> 00:02:50,587
I checked the surroundings.

62
00:02:51,170 --> 00:02:52,547
[CALOY] No one was watching you.

63
00:02:52,630 --> 00:02:53,798
Just me.

64
00:02:54,716 --> 00:02:56,009
I was the only one.

65
00:02:56,092 --> 00:03:01,848
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

66
00:03:01,931 --> 00:03:03,933
[BEA EXHALES DEEPLY]

67
00:03:10,857 --> 00:03:11,733
'Bi…

68
00:03:13,318 --> 00:03:14,360
Are you okay?

69
00:03:14,444 --> 00:03:19,699
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

70
00:03:19,782 --> 00:03:21,451
[SNIFFLES]

71
00:03:25,496 --> 00:03:28,666
[SNIFFLES AGAIN]

72
00:03:29,709 --> 00:03:31,210
[SIGHS]

73
00:03:33,004 --> 00:03:38,927
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

74
00:03:40,970 --> 00:03:42,388
[SIGHS]

75
00:03:43,848 --> 00:03:45,934
[BREATHES DEEPLY]

76
00:03:47,185 --> 00:03:48,895
Caloy, I don't understand.

77
00:03:49,687 --> 00:03:53,483
I've done everything I can

78
00:03:54,192 --> 00:03:56,819
to give my mother a good life.

79
00:03:58,321 --> 00:03:59,322
[BEA SNIFFLES]

80
00:04:00,531 --> 00:04:01,866
What's happening?

81
00:04:02,617 --> 00:04:04,702
I'm back to square one.

82
00:04:04,786 --> 00:04:08,539
I want Billy's life
because it should've been mine.

83
00:04:09,624 --> 00:04:13,211
That should've been mine,
but Billy just had to steal it!

84
00:04:13,294 --> 00:04:19,759
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

85
00:04:25,139 --> 00:04:31,854
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

86
00:05:09,100 --> 00:05:10,393
[LOVELINE AGENT 1]
That's good news.

87
00:05:10,476 --> 00:05:13,938
I'm glad my advice
the last time you called was helpful.

88
00:05:14,814 --> 00:05:16,065
[LOVELINE AGENT 2] Hmm? Yes, Ms. P?

89
00:05:16,149 --> 00:05:18,568
Any update on your concern
about Sir Brandon?

90
00:05:18,651 --> 00:05:20,570
[KEYBOARDS CLACKING]

91
00:05:20,653 --> 00:05:24,240
[LOVELINE AGENT 2] Please don't feel
guilty that you have other priorities.

92
00:05:24,324 --> 00:05:26,117
There is nothing wrong with that.

93
00:05:26,200 --> 00:05:29,454
A healthy relationship
is supposed to be supportive,

94
00:05:29,537 --> 00:05:30,955
not combative.

95
00:05:31,039 --> 00:05:33,166
If you two are arguing most of the time

96
00:05:33,249 --> 00:05:35,168
and you have no time for him,

97
00:05:35,251 --> 00:05:37,920
then maybe it could help
if you can pause and reflect.

98
00:05:38,004 --> 00:05:42,300
So that you can decide
what's best for the both of you.

99
00:05:42,383 --> 00:05:45,094
Right now, Brandon isn't being
persistent anymore.

100
00:05:45,845 --> 00:05:50,183
I just really don't want us
to separate on bad terms.

101
00:05:50,266 --> 00:05:51,142
But…

102
00:05:51,893 --> 00:05:56,647
But if he doesn't want us
to have proper closure,

103
00:05:56,731 --> 00:05:59,025
there's nothing I can do about it, right?

104
00:05:59,108 --> 00:06:00,568
That's right, Ms. P.

105
00:06:01,194 --> 00:06:04,989
Sometimes, the best closure
is no closure at all.

106
00:06:05,615 --> 00:06:09,035
And sometimes, it's best to let
things unfold on their own.

107
00:06:09,786 --> 00:06:11,662
Because most of the time,

108
00:06:11,746 --> 00:06:14,457
things turn out for the better.

109
00:06:14,540 --> 00:06:19,212
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING, FADES]

110
00:06:19,295 --> 00:06:23,341
[BEA SNIFFLING]

111
00:06:24,592 --> 00:06:25,885
[SOBS]

112
00:06:25,968 --> 00:06:27,261
We'll take it back.

113
00:06:27,929 --> 00:06:29,222
Don't worry.

114
00:06:29,305 --> 00:06:30,848
[GRIM MUSIC PLAYING]

115
00:06:30,932 --> 00:06:32,767
Like I've said before,

116
00:06:33,768 --> 00:06:34,977
just use me.

117
00:06:36,104 --> 00:06:38,731
Anything, everything you tell me to do,
I'll do it all.

118
00:06:38,815 --> 00:06:40,316
I'll help you.

119
00:06:42,568 --> 00:06:43,736
I'm here for you.

120
00:06:46,531 --> 00:06:47,782
I'm right here.

121
00:06:47,865 --> 00:06:54,080
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

122
00:07:10,304 --> 00:07:16,227
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

123
00:07:34,412 --> 00:07:40,710
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

124
00:07:46,799 --> 00:07:50,386
Blank times negative 15 equals 75.

125
00:07:50,470 --> 00:07:52,346
- What's this?
- Negative five.

126
00:07:52,430 --> 00:07:54,015
- You sure?
- Yes.

127
00:07:54,098 --> 00:07:55,600
Very good. Correct.

128
00:07:56,809 --> 00:07:58,978
Number ten.
Mm-hmm.

129
00:07:59,061 --> 00:08:02,899
Blank times 13 equals 65.

130
00:08:02,982 --> 00:08:04,442
This one's easy. What's the answer?

131
00:08:05,067 --> 00:08:06,152
Five!

132
00:08:06,819 --> 00:08:08,863
- Very good!
- [GROANING]

133
00:08:08,946 --> 00:08:10,072
Sleepy?

134
00:08:10,156 --> 00:08:11,866
- I'm tired.
- Okay, all right.

135
00:08:11,949 --> 00:08:13,826
Let's call it a day.
Let's do the rest tomorrow.

136
00:08:13,910 --> 00:08:15,161
Very good!

137
00:08:15,244 --> 00:08:16,496
Good night. Teddy!

138
00:08:16,579 --> 00:08:18,331
- Okay. Here you go.
- Thank you!

139
00:08:18,915 --> 00:08:20,416
Go to sleep, okay?

140
00:08:21,459 --> 00:08:23,294
Let's do the rest tomorrow, okay?

141
00:08:23,377 --> 00:08:24,879
- Tomorrow!
- Okay.

142
00:08:24,962 --> 00:08:26,339
- Good night!
- Good night!

143
00:08:26,422 --> 00:08:27,715
Good job!

144
00:08:27,798 --> 00:08:28,883
Very good. [SMOOCHES]

145
00:08:28,966 --> 00:08:34,347
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING, FADES]

146
00:08:38,851 --> 00:08:40,019
Auntie Pres.

147
00:08:40,853 --> 00:08:42,271
You're still up, Billy?

148
00:08:42,355 --> 00:08:43,981
[BILLY] So are you.

149
00:08:44,065 --> 00:08:47,026
[PRECIOUS] My two-week leave
has been approved.

150
00:08:47,109 --> 00:08:48,319
- Wow!
- That means

151
00:08:48,402 --> 00:08:51,781
I can look after Oliver even if
he doesn't want me to.

152
00:08:51,864 --> 00:08:53,324
- [BILLY LAUGHS]
- [PRECIOUS GIGGLING]

153
00:08:53,908 --> 00:08:56,994
Auntie Pres, you can use that time
for yourself too, you know.

154
00:08:58,037 --> 00:08:59,580
For when you want to take a break.

155
00:08:59,664 --> 00:09:00,581
Hm?

156
00:09:00,665 --> 00:09:02,667
And where would I go?

157
00:09:03,417 --> 00:09:04,835
To the mall, or

158
00:09:04,919 --> 00:09:05,962
to the salon!

159
00:09:06,045 --> 00:09:07,088
- That's good too.
- [GIGGLES]

160
00:09:07,171 --> 00:09:09,799
Or to go out on a date!

161
00:09:09,882 --> 00:09:11,634
Hmm…

162
00:09:11,717 --> 00:09:14,178
Do your agents report to you?

163
00:09:14,262 --> 00:09:17,974
Isn't LoveLine supposed
to be a secure line?

164
00:09:18,057 --> 00:09:19,183
Oh, it is, Auntie.

165
00:09:19,267 --> 00:09:21,352
All LoveLine calls are confidential.

166
00:09:21,435 --> 00:09:24,063
- It just so happened that…
- Hmm?

167
00:09:25,106 --> 00:09:28,025
I was doing my rounds when you called.

168
00:09:28,109 --> 00:09:30,987
- It was just a coincidence.
- Okay…

169
00:09:31,070 --> 00:09:34,282
But thank you for trusting LoveLine.

170
00:09:34,365 --> 00:09:36,659
But of course, Billy.

171
00:09:36,742 --> 00:09:38,035
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

172
00:09:38,119 --> 00:09:39,787
So…

173
00:09:39,870 --> 00:09:42,623
Do you… do you want to talk about it?

174
00:09:42,707 --> 00:09:44,000
Hmm…

175
00:09:46,460 --> 00:09:49,797
You know how our family is, right?

176
00:09:49,880 --> 00:09:51,716
- [BILLY] Mm-hmm.
- Family first.

177
00:09:51,799 --> 00:09:54,010
- Mm-hmm.
- If he can't accept that,

178
00:09:54,093 --> 00:09:56,929
then there's nothing we can do about it.

179
00:09:57,972 --> 00:09:59,140
[BILLY] Hmm.

180
00:09:59,223 --> 00:10:03,728
There's no way I'd prioritize
going on dates with Brandon

181
00:10:03,811 --> 00:10:07,231
when Oliver's safety is being
compromised, right?

182
00:10:09,233 --> 00:10:10,901
You know, Billy,

183
00:10:11,986 --> 00:10:16,699
when Rico passed away,
I poured all my love into you and Oliver.

184
00:10:17,450 --> 00:10:18,951
Mm-hmm.

185
00:10:19,035 --> 00:10:20,036
[PRECIOUS CLICKS TONGUE]

186
00:10:20,119 --> 00:10:22,121
And I thought…

187
00:10:24,415 --> 00:10:26,250
I thought that was enough.

188
00:10:26,334 --> 00:10:27,418
Hmm.

189
00:10:30,421 --> 00:10:31,922
Hmm…

190
00:10:33,007 --> 00:10:35,092
So when Brandon came along,

191
00:10:35,176 --> 00:10:38,137
I wasn't really looking for love.

192
00:10:38,220 --> 00:10:41,432
- I wasn't expecting anything.
- Mm-hmm.

193
00:10:41,515 --> 00:10:44,310
[PRECIOUS] When he came along, I thought,

194
00:10:44,393 --> 00:10:47,104
"Oh, maybe I can still meet
someone again."

195
00:10:48,272 --> 00:10:51,150
"Maybe this is it.
Maybe this is my second chance."

196
00:10:51,233 --> 00:10:52,777
[BILLY] Mm.

197
00:10:52,860 --> 00:10:56,364
I'm not getting any younger, you know?

198
00:10:57,657 --> 00:10:58,824
And you…

199
00:10:58,908 --> 00:11:00,743
You already have your own life.

200
00:11:02,995 --> 00:11:04,789
One day, Billy,

201
00:11:04,872 --> 00:11:08,584
you'll meet someone
and start your own family.

202
00:11:08,668 --> 00:11:10,294
That's still a long way off.

203
00:11:11,337 --> 00:11:15,883
As for Oliver, in a few years,
he'll be going abroad,

204
00:11:15,966 --> 00:11:19,970
and he'll be moving out too.

205
00:11:23,891 --> 00:11:25,976
So then I thought, maybe…

206
00:11:27,436 --> 00:11:29,647
Maybe I need to too.

207
00:11:32,149 --> 00:11:35,986
Maybe I need to have a life of my own.

208
00:11:36,070 --> 00:11:39,281
- Since you have your own lives.
- Hmm!

209
00:11:41,909 --> 00:11:44,036
But maybe I don't really
have a love story.

210
00:11:44,120 --> 00:11:46,288
Maybe it's all just in my head.
Maybe I'm just imagining it.

211
00:11:46,372 --> 00:11:48,207
Oh, come on! What are
you talking about, Auntie Pres?

212
00:11:48,290 --> 00:11:50,167
- Don't mind me, gosh.
- Oh, come on!

213
00:11:50,251 --> 00:11:52,086
- With a face like yours?!
- [PRECIOUS] Hmm!

214
00:11:52,169 --> 00:11:53,921
- You're kind and caring.
- Stop!

215
00:11:54,004 --> 00:11:55,631
- You're smart and a good cook!
- Hey, Benilda!

216
00:11:55,714 --> 00:11:58,175
- Stop it.
- Seriously?!

217
00:11:58,259 --> 00:11:59,343
Hmm?

218
00:11:59,427 --> 00:12:01,846
- It's impossible.
- Mm-hmm, mm-hmm.

219
00:12:03,264 --> 00:12:04,473
- You know, Auntie Pres?
- Hmm?

220
00:12:04,557 --> 00:12:07,435
I've heard so many love stories

221
00:12:07,518 --> 00:12:09,228
- on LoveList.
- Hmm.

222
00:12:09,311 --> 00:12:14,275
But do you know whose love story
I'm most excited about?

223
00:12:15,651 --> 00:12:16,735
Yours.

224
00:12:18,737 --> 00:12:23,742
Because you're someone
who gives so, so much love.

225
00:12:23,826 --> 00:12:28,080
So I'm sure you'll get
so, so much love in return.

226
00:12:29,081 --> 00:12:30,624
[CHUCKLES SLIGHTLY, SNIFFLES]

227
00:12:30,708 --> 00:12:33,919
Have faith, Auntie. If you and Brandon
don't work out, so be it.

228
00:12:34,003 --> 00:12:37,339
But if you're meant to be, then you are.

229
00:12:39,341 --> 00:12:41,218
Oh, Billy.

230
00:12:41,927 --> 00:12:43,554
You know, I don't want to
think about it for now.

231
00:12:43,637 --> 00:12:46,557
Honestly, what we're
going through is no joke.

232
00:12:46,640 --> 00:12:49,310
Anyway, what's the latest
with Caloy and Bea?

233
00:12:50,144 --> 00:12:51,520
Uh…

234
00:12:51,604 --> 00:12:53,898
Well, hmm…

235
00:12:53,981 --> 00:12:56,901
They still haven't found Caloy.

236
00:12:56,984 --> 00:12:59,361
As for Bea, the case is still pending.

237
00:13:00,362 --> 00:13:01,739
Don't worry, Billy.

238
00:13:02,364 --> 00:13:04,575
We'll protect each other.

239
00:13:05,993 --> 00:13:07,119
Always.

240
00:13:07,203 --> 00:13:08,579
[BRIGHT MUSIC PLAYING]

241
00:13:08,662 --> 00:13:10,206
Oh, enough with the flattery.

242
00:13:10,289 --> 00:13:11,665
- Just help me instead.
- You want that?

243
00:13:11,749 --> 00:13:12,625
You want a hug?

244
00:13:12,708 --> 00:13:14,376
- Sure, hug this.
- Okay.

245
00:13:14,460 --> 00:13:17,463
[BOTH LAUGHING]

246
00:13:17,546 --> 00:13:19,673
[MOTORCYCLE ENGINE REVVING]

247
00:13:19,757 --> 00:13:22,218
Okay, dude. Here's what I found.

248
00:13:22,301 --> 00:13:25,971
Bea's mom's name is Mariela Mercado.

249
00:13:27,264 --> 00:13:28,891
This is her hospital record.

250
00:13:29,850 --> 00:13:34,313
She was confined for three years
in a mental institution.

251
00:13:35,231 --> 00:13:37,024
I called the hospital.

252
00:13:37,107 --> 00:13:42,029
Unfortunately,
all the records are strictly confidential.

253
00:13:42,112 --> 00:13:46,909
But at least we know that her mother
has a history of mental illness.

254
00:13:46,992 --> 00:13:48,869
That's serious, Jordan.

255
00:13:50,287 --> 00:13:53,040
Maybe she really needs professional help.

256
00:13:53,123 --> 00:13:54,542
That's what I'm saying, dude.

257
00:13:55,918 --> 00:13:57,836
But there's nothing we can do right now

258
00:13:58,504 --> 00:14:00,839
except be careful.

259
00:14:01,840 --> 00:14:03,092
Thank you, Jordan.

260
00:14:03,717 --> 00:14:04,760
Anytime.

261
00:14:05,469 --> 00:14:11,684
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

262
00:14:14,353 --> 00:14:20,526
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

263
00:14:35,666 --> 00:14:41,589
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

264
00:14:49,513 --> 00:14:50,389
[LINE RINGING]

265
00:14:52,892 --> 00:14:59,565
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

266
00:15:09,909 --> 00:15:16,540
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

267
00:15:21,128 --> 00:15:22,212
Yes, sir.

268
00:15:22,296 --> 00:15:24,048
She's still outside.

269
00:15:24,131 --> 00:15:25,424
Are you on your way?

270
00:15:26,258 --> 00:15:27,927
Okay, please hurry.

271
00:15:33,599 --> 00:15:34,725
[DOOR CLOSES SOFTLY]

272
00:15:39,813 --> 00:15:41,023
[SOFTLY] Auntie Pres?

273
00:15:41,941 --> 00:15:43,233
- [BILLY] Auntie?
- [PRECIOUS] Mm?

274
00:15:43,317 --> 00:15:45,235
- Auntie Pres, sorry.
- [PRECIOUS GRUNTS]

275
00:15:45,319 --> 00:15:46,320
[PRECIOUS] Mm?

276
00:15:46,987 --> 00:15:49,907
A woman has been standing outside
for a while now.

277
00:15:51,116 --> 00:15:52,159
Is it Bea?

278
00:15:52,242 --> 00:15:57,122
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC
PLAYING]

279
00:15:57,206 --> 00:15:58,332
I can't make her out clearly.

280
00:15:58,415 --> 00:16:00,167
- I'll check it out.
- No, you won't!

281
00:16:00,250 --> 00:16:03,003
- Let's just call the police!
- They're already on their way.

282
00:16:03,087 --> 00:16:04,171
- Huh?
- I'll bring this with me.

283
00:16:04,254 --> 00:16:05,965
Just wait a minute, Auntie.

284
00:16:07,800 --> 00:16:11,804
[DOOR CREAKING]

285
00:16:16,016 --> 00:16:22,231
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

286
00:16:24,400 --> 00:16:26,068
[LINE RINGING]

287
00:16:26,151 --> 00:16:27,403
Hello? Chief?

288
00:16:27,486 --> 00:16:29,405
[OFFICER] <i>Ma'am, are you</i>
<i>the one who called earlier?</i>

289
00:16:29,488 --> 00:16:31,532
Yes, it's me. Where are you right now?

290
00:16:31,615 --> 00:16:33,075
[OFFICER] <i>We're already near, ma'am.</i>

291
00:16:33,158 --> 00:16:34,910
Okay. Please hurry up.

292
00:16:34,994 --> 00:16:35,953
Thank you.

293
00:16:36,036 --> 00:16:37,454
Why did you call the police?

294
00:16:38,831 --> 00:16:40,499
I didn't come here to make a scene.

295
00:16:40,582 --> 00:16:43,752
Ms. Mariela, please leave.

296
00:16:44,712 --> 00:16:47,089
Billy, have mercy on me and my daughter.

297
00:16:49,174 --> 00:16:50,467
[MARIELA] Let me in.

298
00:16:50,551 --> 00:16:52,720
I'm just going to talk with you.

299
00:16:53,762 --> 00:16:54,888
[PRECIOUS] Billy.

300
00:16:54,972 --> 00:17:01,061
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

301
00:17:02,730 --> 00:17:03,689
Ma?

302
00:17:11,488 --> 00:17:12,614
Ma?

303
00:17:17,286 --> 00:17:18,245
Ma?

304
00:17:18,328 --> 00:17:25,044
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

305
00:17:34,053 --> 00:17:35,888
MAMA

306
00:17:37,431 --> 00:17:40,642
[OUT OF SERVICE TONE]

307
00:17:44,104 --> 00:17:45,856
[OUT OF SERVICE TONE]

308
00:17:45,939 --> 00:17:46,857
[EXHALES SHARPLY]

309
00:17:46,940 --> 00:17:53,614
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

310
00:18:04,249 --> 00:18:06,293
All I have is Bea now.

311
00:18:06,376 --> 00:18:08,128
My husband abandoned us.

312
00:18:08,712 --> 00:18:10,130
My eldest child

313
00:18:11,340 --> 00:18:13,050
has passed away already.

314
00:18:14,051 --> 00:18:17,513
[SNIFFLES] I won't be able to handle it
if I also lose Bea.

315
00:18:17,596 --> 00:18:20,516
Your daughter is the one
who started this mess.

316
00:18:20,599 --> 00:18:22,684
Please, have some empathy.

317
00:18:23,393 --> 00:18:24,812
She has done nothing wrong.

318
00:18:24,895 --> 00:18:27,481
She was just jealous of her sister,

319
00:18:27,564 --> 00:18:29,441
so she pretended to be Abi.

320
00:18:29,525 --> 00:18:32,319
Ms. Mariela, this isn't just about her
pretending to be Abi.

321
00:18:32,402 --> 00:18:34,655
Your daughter had our system hacked

322
00:18:34,738 --> 00:18:36,740
before she even applied to our company.

323
00:18:36,824 --> 00:18:38,575
I hope you understand that.

324
00:18:38,659 --> 00:18:41,370
Don't accuse her of that!

325
00:18:41,453 --> 00:18:42,871
You don't have any proof!

326
00:18:42,955 --> 00:18:44,540
Wait a minute.

327
00:18:44,623 --> 00:18:46,542
How well do you even know your child?

328
00:18:46,625 --> 00:18:50,712
We are certain that Bea ordered Caloy
to trespass into our house!

329
00:18:50,796 --> 00:18:53,215
My child was hurt
because of their actions!

330
00:18:53,298 --> 00:18:56,051
Actually, Caloy and your child
should be in prison!

331
00:18:56,135 --> 00:18:57,261
Liar!

332
00:18:57,344 --> 00:19:01,473
I understand that as a mother,
you just want to protect your child.

333
00:19:01,557 --> 00:19:03,142
But what she's doing is wrong.

334
00:19:03,934 --> 00:19:05,477
And as parents,

335
00:19:05,561 --> 00:19:07,437
shouldn't we teach our children
to do what's right?

336
00:19:07,521 --> 00:19:09,773
We shouldn't be covering up for them.

337
00:19:09,857 --> 00:19:12,067
But here you are, lying for your child!

338
00:19:12,151 --> 00:19:14,987
What are you trying to say?
That I'm a bad mother?

339
00:19:15,070 --> 00:19:16,905
I didn't say that.

340
00:19:16,989 --> 00:19:18,699
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

341
00:19:19,283 --> 00:19:21,827
Billy, you're already rich!

342
00:19:22,411 --> 00:19:24,538
Your life is so good!

343
00:19:24,621 --> 00:19:26,707
But my daughter…

344
00:19:26,790 --> 00:19:28,584
She just asked for help.

345
00:19:28,667 --> 00:19:31,128
She made some small mistakes.

346
00:19:31,211 --> 00:19:32,963
And you already want her to go to jail?!

347
00:19:34,965 --> 00:19:36,341
[WHIMPERS]

348
00:19:36,425 --> 00:19:38,343
Don't you have a heart?

349
00:19:38,969 --> 00:19:43,015
[MARIELA] You have no empathy!
Not even a little bit.

350
00:19:43,098 --> 00:19:46,435
We're just asking for some compassion.

351
00:19:46,518 --> 00:19:53,150
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

352
00:19:55,068 --> 00:20:00,574
<i>Please have some mercy</i>
<i>and empathy, Billy.</i>

353
00:20:00,657 --> 00:20:03,744
<i>I'm sorry, but I really can't</i>
<i>overlook Abi's actions.</i>

354
00:20:03,827 --> 00:20:06,121
<i>Your life will change,</i>
<i>you bastard!</i>

355
00:20:06,205 --> 00:20:07,372
<i>You'll suffer!</i>

356
00:20:07,456 --> 00:20:10,792
<i>I can't bear to see you</i>
<i>suffer, my dear.</i>

357
00:20:10,876 --> 00:20:12,002
<i>I'm not suffering.</i>

358
00:20:12,085 --> 00:20:13,837
<i>I never said that</i>
<i>I was suffering.</i>

359
00:20:13,921 --> 00:20:16,673
<i>I promise you.</i>
<i>I'll get back at Billy.</i>

360
00:20:16,757 --> 00:20:17,925
<i>Could you come with me?</i>

361
00:20:18,008 --> 00:20:22,095
<i>Is there really no way</i>
<i>we can look at Mariela Mercado's files?</i>

362
00:20:22,179 --> 00:20:24,932
<i>I'm really sorry, ma'am,</i>
<i>but you can't.</i>

363
00:20:25,015 --> 00:20:26,558
<i>Those are confidential.</i>

364
00:20:27,142 --> 00:20:29,728
[BILLY] <i>Did you know that her mother</i>
<i>has a burn scar on her head?</i>

365
00:20:29,811 --> 00:20:31,396
<i>Bea has a huge grudge against you.</i>

366
00:20:31,480 --> 00:20:33,482
[BILLY] <i>I hope we finally learn why.</i>

367
00:20:33,565 --> 00:20:36,235
<i>My family's safety is at stake here.</i>

368
00:20:36,318 --> 00:20:37,694
<i>Oliver's lucky to have you.</i>

369
00:20:37,778 --> 00:20:41,323
<i>Oh, I'm the one who's lucky</i>
<i>to have him and his sister.</i>

370
00:20:44,826 --> 00:20:47,287
<i>29 Evangeline Street, Valencia.</i>

371
00:20:48,080 --> 00:20:50,374
<i>This was Bea's old house.</i>

372
00:20:50,457 --> 00:20:54,086
[WOMAN] <i>The rumor is that</i>
<i>Mariela's husband left her.</i>
